From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: log command-path CMD53 transmit result

Record the CMD53 write used by ESP-Hosted control commands.  Together with
the existing receive/IRQ evidence, this distinguishes a host write failure
from a C6 response/interrupt failure.  The record contains only address,
length, and return code.

---
 sdio/esp_sdio.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdio/esp_sdio.c b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -681,6 +681,8 @@ static int tx_process(void *data)
 		do {
 			block_cnt = data_left / ESP_BLOCK_SIZE;
 			len_to_send = data_left;
+			esp_info("CMD53_TX: addr=0x%x bytes=%u\n",
+				 ESP_SLAVE_CMD53_END_ADDR - len_to_send, len_to_send);
 			ret = esp_write_block(context, ESP_SLAVE_CMD53_END_ADDR - len_to_send,
 					pos, (len_to_send + 3) & (~3), ACQUIRE_LOCK);
 
-- 
2.43.0
